# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker build-context excludes.
#
# Both images (api.Dockerfile, web.Dockerfile) use the repo root as context and do
# `COPY . .` → `turbo prune` → fresh `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` → framework
# build INSIDE the image. So none of the host's installed deps or build outputs
# belong in the context. Without this file the context was ~2 GB (node_modules +
# .turbo + .next + .git) and every deploy crawled (~20 min just to transfer +
# rebuild context). NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are injected as `--build-arg` (see the
# `build.args` block in docker-compose.prod.yml), NOT read from a context .env,
# so excluding env files here is safe and keeps secrets out of image layers.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Installed dependencies — reinstalled fresh in the image
**/node_modules

# Framework build outputs & caches — rebuilt in the image
**/.next
**/.turbo
.turbo
**/dist
apps/mobile/build
apps/mobile/.dart_tool

# Secrets & local env — must never enter an image layer (NEXT_PUBLIC_* come via build args)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS / CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Editor / OS / logs / coverage noise
.vscode
.idea
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage

# Build/infra docs not needed inside the runtime images
**/*.md
